       Q: Is there a maximum acceptable production rate or machine-speed multiplier above which the optimizer must not go, even if doing so would improve value/resource? For example, would running at 130% of nominal cycle rate to squeeze out more throughput be acceptable, given that empirical data suggest this raises noise by ~6 dB and fatigue by ~0.15 index points per hour?
