    5. noise_level threshold — measurement type (peak vs. time-weighted average)
       Q: The 80 dB(A) limit is attributed to ISO 9612, which defines a time-weighted average (TWA) over the measurement period — but transient machine events can spike well above 80 dB(A) for seconds; should the constraint be applied as an 8-hour TWA (allowing brief peaks) or as a continuous instantaneous never-exceed limit, and if TWA, over what window (full shift or rolling 15-minute block)?
       A: Apply 80 dB(A) as the shift-long 8-hour TWA in accordance with ISO 9612 § 8; a secondary instantaneous ceiling of 85 dB(A) is added to prevent very short high-intensity bursts, consistent with EU Directive 2003/10/EC exposure action values.

