       A: A minimum of one 10-minute rest break every 2 hours and one 30-minute meal break within the shift are enforced as hard structural constraints, consistent with standard ergonomic guidance, regardless of the cumulative fatigue index value.
    5. workplace_noise_level / noise measurement averaging window
       Q: Should the 80 dB(A) limit apply only to the shift-level time-averaged LAeq, or must it also prevent instantaneous peaks exceeding 80 dB(A) at any moment during the shift? Time-averaging permits short high-noise events (e.g., machine start-ups or reconfigurations) that could still contribute to hearing-damage risk even when the average remains compliant.
       A: The 80 dB(A) limit is applied to the shift-level LAeq time average only. Instantaneous peaks are not separately constrained unless a regulatory requirement is subsequently identified, at which time a peak ceiling (e.g., 85 dB(A) instantaneous) would be added as an additional hard constraint.

